cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fashion-RQBench, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "Fashion-RQBench: A Four-Task Retrieval Benchmark over Hierarchical Semantic IDs"
abstract: >-
  Fashion-RQBench is a four-task benchmark for retrieval and ranking over a
  hierarchical semantic-ID item space. Items are tokenized into three-level
  semantic IDs by an RQ-VAE trained with a per-level attribute exclusivity loss;
  natural-language queries are authored per SID cluster from that cluster's
  attribute distribution, giving every query a ground-truth item set derived
  from the hierarchy. The release contains 588 clusters, 5,807 queries and four
  tasks (query-product ranking, hierarchical relevance classification, sibling
  discrimination, query paraphrase robustness).
